Sval: ignore audio playback messages for a browser that has gone

AudioPlaybackParent.receiveMessage reads the tab's browser from
browsingContext.top.embedderElement, which is null once the tab has
closed, and an AudioPlayback:Stop sent as a playing tab closes arrives
after that. It throws, logging a console error for every tab closed
while it plays sound. didDestroy already guards the same lookup.

AudioPlaybackChild sends the same message from the "audio-playback"
observer, which can run once its window global can no longer send, and
sendAsyncMessage then throws InvalidStateError.

diff --git a/toolkit/actors/AudioPlaybackChild.sys.mjs b/toolkit/actors/AudioPlaybackChild.sys.mjs
index 6d30d10f25..4504ab3b1d 100644
--- a/toolkit/actors/AudioPlaybackChild.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/actors/AudioPlaybackChild.sys.mjs
@@ -13,7 +13,11 @@ export class AudioPlaybackChild extends JSWindowActorChild {
       } else {
         name += data === "active" ? "Start" : "Stop";
       }
-      this.sendAsyncMessage(name);
+      try {
+        this.sendAsyncMessage(name);
+      } catch {
+        // The window is going away, and its parent with it.
+      }
     }
   }
 }
